# {{ linkmo_dir }}

A command line and an HTTP API over the `{{ project_slug }}` LinkML schema and its data. Both are built from the schema when they start: one command and one endpoint per exposed class, with one filter per slot of the class. Nothing is generated into this folder ahead of time, so a slot added to the schema is a filter at the next start.

The linkmo copier template made this project beside the LinkML sidecar in `{{ sidecar_dir or '.' }}/`. It reads the schema from `{{ schema_path }}` and the records from {% if data_source == 'yaml' %}the YAML files under `{{ data_path }}`{% else %}`{{ data_object }}`{% endif %}.

## Use it

From the host root:

```bash
just --justfile {{ linkmo_dir }}/justfile install          # uv sync, once
just --justfile {{ linkmo_dir }}/justfile cli --help       # the command line, {{ command_name }}
just --justfile {{ linkmo_dir }}/justfile serve            # the API on http://localhost:8000/docs
just --justfile {{ linkmo_dir }}/justfile test
```

Inside this folder, plain `just <recipe>` works, and after `just install` so does `uv run {{ command_name }} --help`. `just --list` shows the rest: the published contract, a web UI's entity list, the SSSOM check, the Datasette browse database and the schema's pages with examples.
{% if schema_path.startswith('pkg:') or (data_source == 'yaml' and data_path.startswith('pkg:')) %}
A `pkg:` path is read from an installed package{% if requirements %}, which `just install` installs as `{{ requirements | join('`, `') }}`{% endif %}. To use an environment that already has the package, set `LINKMO_PYTHON` to its Python, and the recipes put `src/` on its path.{% if requirements %} Answer `requirements` with `[]` to leave the package out of this project's dependencies.{% endif %}
{% endif %}
A command lists the records of its class. Give an identifier to fetch one record, any option to filter, `--count` for the number only, and `--mode api` to ask a running server instead of reading the data in the process. The API answers `GET /<class>` with the same parameters and the same JSON, and publishes its contract at `/openapi.json`.

## What is yours

The template created these files once and never overwrites them:

- `{{ exposure_file }}` says which classes are exposed, under which path, and binds hand-written operations to paths.
- `src/{{ python_package }}/hand.py` holds those operations.
- `tests/expected_counts.yaml` lists the questions your data must answer and how many records each returns.
- `project.justfile` holds your own recipes.

Everything else follows the template. Run `copier update -a .copier-answers.linkmo.yml --trust` from the host root to bring in a new version. It updates this template on its own and does not touch the sidecar.
